un data quality assertions (e.g., verifying transaction_amount is never negative) before writing to final production schemas.Step 5: Automated Deployment & Monitoring (The Platform Layer)Infrastructure as Code (IaC): Write Terraform modules to provision your entire stack—S3 buckets, IAM roles, Kubernetes namespaces, and access keys.CI/CD: Use GitHub Actions or GitLab CI to build a pipeline that runs unit tests on your Spark code, validates your dbt models, and automatically packages and deploys your Airflow DAGs when code changes are pushed to your repository.What to put on your GitHub Profile / ResumeTo make this project stand out to hiring managers, highlight these exact technical takeaways:"Built a production-grade DataOps pipeline processing X events/sec utilizing Apache Spark Streaming and Apache Iceberg, reducing analytical storage query latencies via optimized file compaction.""Implemented Data SecOps protocols by integrating HashiCorp Vault with distributed Spark tasks to mask sensitive customer PII dynamically at the ingestion layer.""Designed full Infrastructure as Code (IaC) setup using Terraform to spin up an ephemeral data architecture, reducing cloud infrastructure spend through automated lifecycle policies."Would you like me to help you draft the Docker Compose file or the initial Python script to kick off your mock streaming generator for this project?





